  "summary": "Security-research / proof-of-concept package: verify-cli (npm)",
  "details": "The preinstall hook of verify-cli@99.0.0 runs index.js, which executes a curl command that POSTs host metadata and credential files to the remote host hxxp://5f8a1ed70fb7761d678agw9bucryyyyyb[.]oast[.]site/verify-cli/$(whoami)/$(hostname)/. The request exfiltrates the current username and hostname, and base64-encodes the contents of /etc/passwd, /etc/hosts, the `id` command output, and /etc/shadow (when readable) into the request. The package also depends on the known-malicious package noderedacteddk.",
